    "title": "Hadnot tallies 28 points as Dons top Eastern Michigan - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Glenn Marini ,\n1 hours ago\nFORT WAYNE, Ind. (WANE) – Corey Hadnot II scored a game-high 28 points as the Mastodons topped visiting Eastern Michigan 80-65 at the Coliseum on Wednesday night.\nDeandre Craig Jr. tallied 15 points while former South Side Archer Mikale Stevenson chipped in with 13 points for the Dons, who shot 50 percent (28-of-56) from the floor as a team.\nThe Dons improve to 6-6 overall this season with their next game set for Sunday at home against Detroit Mercy at 5 pm at the Coliseum,\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
